\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Approach, my soul, the mercy seat,
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0  Where Jesus answers prayer;
\par  There, humbly fall before His feet,
\par  For none can perish there.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Thy promise is my only plea;
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0  With this, I venture nigh;
\par  Thou callest burdened souls to Thee,
\par  And as such, O Lord, am I.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   Bowed down beneath a load of sin,
\par \pard\li225\sl188\slmult0  By satan sorely pressed,
\par \pard\li270\sl188\slmult0  By war without and fears within,
\par  I come to thee for rest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Be Thou my shield and hiding place,
\par \pard\li270\sl188\slmult0   That, sheltered near Thy side,
\par  I may, my fierce accuser face,
\par  And tell him Thou hast died.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl188\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   O wondrous love! To bleed and die,
\par \pard\li270\sl188\slmult0   To bear the cross and shame,
\par   That guilty sinners, such as I,\tab 
\par \pard       Might plead Thy gracious name!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

